# Qt 6.11.3 hold for every hard image (moved here from nvidia/resolver-holds 2026-10-31, where
# it served nvidiahard only). Every hard rootfs and the host run Qt 6.11.2-r2.
#
# 10-28: ::gentoo had no pyside-6.11.3, so 6.11.3 was a slot conflict across the whole Qt set.
# 10-31: pyside-6.11.3 exists, but the move still does not happen: the installed KF6 6.31
# and the Plasma 6.8.2 binpkgs are bound to the qtbase 6.11.2 subslot. amdkdehard pass 1
# ('update-seed') exhausted --backtrack=30 on it and aborted with a Qt-wide slot conflict;
# at --backtrack=100 it resolved in 384 s / 41 backtracks by SKIPPING Qt 6.11.3 anyway.
# This hold gives that same plan without the backtracking.
#
# Lift when the host takes Qt 6.11.3 (binpkgs at the new subslot then exist), or run the
# move on purpose as its own pass: emerge -1 the dev-qt set + pyside + the := consumers.
>=dev-qt/qt3d-6.11.3:6
